---
description: Keep Nova database credentials and API keys out of source code
alwaysApply: true
---

# Secrets

- Store real database URLs, passwords, tokens and API keys only in the ignored root `.env` file.
- Read credentials through environment variables on the server. Never hardcode, log, commit, or return them to clients.
- Never use a `VITE_` prefix for a secret; Vite exposes those variables to the browser.
- Keep `.env.example` limited to empty values and documentation.
- When running database commands, sanitize failures so connection URLs are not printed.
